.TH PART 5
.SH NAME
part \- solid part source
.SH DESCRIPTION
A solid part source holds the statements of the programs of a pipe,
.IR extrude (1),
.IR bool (1)
and
.IR fillet (1),
in the language of
.IR plicad (7).
Each program takes its own statements, and passes the others on in
the stream it writes
.RI ( stream (5));
the definitions and the sets of faces stay for every program.
.I U
and
.I v
are the two axes other than
.IR a ,
in alphabetical order.
.TP
.BI profile " name " along " a u v r"
.RB [ side
.IR side ]
.RI [ "u v r" " ...]"
.br
.BI corner " u v r"
.RB [ side
.IR side ]
.RI [ "u v r" " ...]"
.br
A closed outline in the plane across the world axis
.IR a ,
its corners in order, each rounded by an arc of radius
.I r
(sharp for 0); corner lines continue it.
.B side
after a corner names the side from it to the next corner.
.TP
.BI circle " name d u v " along " a"
A circle of diameter
.I d
about
.RI ( u ,
.IR v ).
.TP
.BI extrude " name " from " w0 " to " w1 p"
.RB [ draft
.IR deg ]
.RB [ pattern
.I ax n p
.RI [ "ax n p" ]]
.br
The solid of profile
.I p
from
.I w0
to
.I w1
along its axis.
With a draft (0 to 89 degrees) each side leans inward;
with a pattern,
.I n
copies are made,
.I p
apart along the signed axis, as one solid.
Its faces are named
.IB name .start ,
.IB name .end ,
.IB name .side. side
for a named side of the profile, and
.IB name .side
for the other sides and the arcs of the corners.
.TP
.BI union " name a b"
.RI [ c " ...]"
.br
.BI subtract " name a b"
.RI [ c " ...]"
.br
.BI common " name a b"
.br
Replace the named solids by the solid
.I name
(their union,
.I a
less the others, or their common part).
The faces keep their names.
.TP
.BI faces " set ref"
.RI [ ref " ...]"
A set of faces, for the rules below and for the pins of
.IR mold (1).
.TP
.BI round " r " convex
.br
.BI round " r ref ref"
.br
.BI sharp " ref ref"
.br
Give a radius to the outward edges, or to the edges between two faces
that the references name.
Of the rules for an edge, the last applies; sharp is radius 0.
A rule that names no edge is refused.
The face of a round is named after the two faces it joins, with a +
between them.
.TP
.BI finish " material ref"
.RI [ ref " ...]"
Give the faces that the references name the finish of the material,
.IR plicad (7):
a texture of the mold, with the least draft it needs, which
.IR mold (1)
checks, and a tint in
.IR tomesh (1).
Of the finishes of a face the last applies; a face with none keeps
that of the body of the part, its base.
.TP
.BI thread " ref"
.RB [ deep
.IR d ]
.I designation ...
.br
Give the holes of the faces that the reference names a thread, as
.BR "thread taps 4-40 UNC-2B" :
the solid has them at the tap drill, and drawings call out the
designation, through or to the depth
.I d
from the mouth of the hole, or for a blind hole without one, to its
depth
.RI ( smview (1)).
Of the threads of a face the last applies.
.TP
.BI material " ..."
.br
.BI materials " file"
The materials of the finishes, as
.IR plicad (7)
says, for
.IR mold (1),
which runs before
.IR place (1)
gives the part its materials.
.PP
A reference
.I ref
names the faces that the source declares:
.TP
.B any
every face;
.TP
.I set
the faces of a set;
.TP
.I name
every face of the solid that extrude made as
.IR name ;
.TP
.IB name .start ", " name .end ", " name .side
its ends, or all its sides;
.TP
.IB name . side
the side of its profile named
.IR side .
.PP
A face of a round matches what either face it joins matches.
.SH EXAMPLE
.RS
.nf
profile r along z 0 0 0 side front 20 0 0 20 10 0 0 10 0
extrude blk from 0 to 5 r
circle c 6 10 5 along z
extrude boss from 5 to 8 c
union u blk boss
round 1 blk.front blk.end
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
plicad(7), extrude(1), bool(1), fillet(1), mold(1), stream(5)
